[ext_resource type="Resource" path="res://data/loot/ShopLeveledGear.tres" id="3_leveled"]

; Hesk the Wayfarer (Phase 38J) — the first merchant in the game who is not always there.
;
; He is in the Ember Crown one day in four (VisitEveryDays = 4, VisitDayOffset = 1) and trades
; 09:00–17:00 on the day he is. Presence is a pure function of WorldClock.Day, so unlike every other
; piece of shop state in this arc he needs NOTHING in the save: a fact you can recompute has no
; timeline to drift out of.
;
; What makes him worth waiting for is the BUY side, not the shelf. He deals in what the Ember Crown has
; no use for — pelts, trophies, gemstones, fine goods — and pays a specialist's premium for all four,
; against the biggest purse in the realm. A player who has been hauling beast pelts around a farming
; village and being offered a plain price by Aldreth has a reason to check what day it is.
;
; ⚠️ NOT A SINGLE CONSUMABLE on his shelves, and that is a rule rather than a taste: --validate rejects
; a consumable sold only by travelling shops. Hours are a wait — sleep at the inn and the clock moves —
; but a merchant who might not be in town is a coin flip against the calendar, and a player out of
; potions cannot sleep their way to one.
;
; He carries the realm's SECOND leveled pool, which 38B deliberately refused to Bryn ("a second one
; halves how special it is"). That argument was about a second *resident* shelf standing open every day.
; A pool rolled for a trader who is here a quarter of the time is the opposite: it is the reason to
; catch him, and it cannot be shopped until something Legendary appears because he leaves.
;
; RestockDays = 4 matches his cycle: he arrives with a fresh cart and a full purse, which is the
; simplest thing that can be true and needs no new machinery — 38B's clock already carries the shelves,
; the purse and (38H) the appetite.

